answer-field/id #uuid "14205708-8ff3-5fa8-9eb8-23be718d348d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344527}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e7cd9fb4-2876-5e19-b299-1938e7390f38" :question/math-academy-id "q-75479" :question/problem "Calculate the product $Q{I}_{2}$ given that ${I}_{2}$ is the $2\\times 2$ identity matrix and\n$Q=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "Any matrix, when multiplied by an identity matrix, remains unchanged (assuming that the multiplication is well defined).\n\nThe matrix $Q$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix and ${I}_{2}$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix too. \n\nTherefore, the multiplication is well defined and \n\n$$\nQ\\cdot {I}_{2}=Q=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393535 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dd4048bd-c9fc-58bc-85a9-fa6ee2d8ec2b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 5 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393537} {:answer/id #uuid "f10797c4-7b7c-554a-bc06-d36b649490ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 5 & -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393538} {:answer/id #uuid "c82d547a-10f8-58eb-92f2-1b5b12006cb2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 5 & 6 \\\\ 4 & 5 & 6 \\\\ 4 & 5 & 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393539} {:answer/id #uuid "dbf9276b-4afd-5283-aee0-85c974e49bba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 4 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393540} {:answer/id #uuid "b723c812-ba14-5f39-9709-b2ac9879e329" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 5 & 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393541}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393537} :answer-field/id #uuid "953bbaf6-0705-557f-84cb-45da3a319c9c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393536}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "64bbd1d6-4392-5158-946b-c984a6aea3c7" :question/math-academy-id "q-75474" :question/problem "Calculate the product ${I}_{3}K$ given that ${I}_{3}$ is the $3\\times 3$ identity matrix and\n$K=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 5 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "Any matrix, when multiplied by an identity matrix, remains unchanged (assuming that the multiplication is well defined).\n\nThe matrix ${I}_{3}$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $K$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix too. \n\nTherefore, the multiplication is well defined and \n\n$$\n{I}_{3}\\cdot K=K=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 5 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Multiplying a Matrix by the Identity Matrix"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100876 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100697 :question/id #uuid "9832238f-baff-5527-a11a-c65b6529cb0b" :question/math-academy-id "e-4410" :question/problem "Calculate the product $C D,$ if\n![](images/94/945664c408577aac1d1a745120b3c17c46fd9db93e6d26cc53a4e501390936e2.png)\nand \n![](images/90/907ffa0b29d96249fe03a7fce3fe682c08982b14c7b7f72840540e6269196425.png)" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $D$ is the $2$nd *column* of the identity matrix $I_3.$\n\nSince we're multiplying the $3\\times 3$ matrix $C$ by the $2$nd *column* of the identity matrix $I_3,$ the result must be the $2$nd *column* of $C.$ Therefore,\n\n![](images/98/980ae75452824b4a8aa701b4e11be8c31448557933357458329f0a2b73a1cca6.png)\n\nDon't believe it? Let's check the long way:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CD & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 5 & 4 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2\\cdot 0+1\\cdot 1+0\\cdot 0 \\\\ -1\\cdot 0+1\\cdot 1+(-4)\\cdot 0 \\\\ 5\\cdot 0+4\\cdot 1+(-2)\\cdot 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "89362140-1a17-56fd-a9ab-4da336112bee" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050825}] :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186546095 :question-generator/id #uuid "f90de4b9-eae0-5d75-89ef-ff61bc2ec28a" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186100876.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101407 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e77b0e35-b8ea-5618-ab6c-8503315df0e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3.5 \\\\ -2.5 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392443} {:answer/id #uuid "b90bbe8b-d8e5-5080-9aa2-4142743a4b96" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2\\sqrt{7} \\\\ -2 \\\\ \\sqrt{3}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392444} {:answer/id #uuid "6b52aa96-4f70-58ea-b2cf-28f779b7b43b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2\\sqrt{5} & -2.5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392445} {:answer/id #uuid "d06d67b6-8acb-58a8-957c-d55d012736a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 2\\sqrt{5} \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392446} {:answer/id #uuid "e47cb90f-8189-59b3-96b0-469513eb54fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2\\sqrt{7} & -3 & 3.5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392447}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186392444} :answer-field/id #uuid "3cb1f592-094a-5b91-bac8-80971fe96ac3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392442}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "bde0cdd0-7dbe-5ba4-9b36-e66cfe099501" :question/math-academy-id "q-41949" :question/problem "Find the product $AB$, if\n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}2\\sqrt{7} & -3 & 3.5 \\\\ -2 & 2\\sqrt{5} & -2.5 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 4 & 5\\end{bmatrix}$\nand \n$B=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $B$ is the $1$st *column* of the identity matrix ${I}_{3}.$\n\nSince we're multiplying the $3\\times 3$ matrix $A$ by the $1$st *column* of the identity matrix ${I}_{3},$ the result must be the $1$st *column* of $A.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\nAB=\\begin{bmatrix}2\\sqrt{7} \\\\ -2 \\\\ \\sqrt{3}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nLet's check the long way:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =\\begin{bmatrix}2\\sqrt{7} & -3 & 3.5 \\\\ -2 & 2\\sqrt{5} & -2.5 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 4 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2\\sqrt{7}\\cdot 1+(-3)\\cdot 0+3.5\\cdot 0 \\\\ (-2)\\cdot 1+2\\sqrt{5}\\cdot 0+(-2.5)\\cdot 0 \\\\ \\sqrt{3}\\cdot 1+4\\cdot 0+5\\cdot 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2\\sqrt{7} \\\\ -2 \\\\ \\sqrt{3}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101408 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "be5f5e04-2f01-53f2-8591-c58133cd71f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -3 \\\\ \\sqrt{5}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099610} {:answer/id #uuid "cea56a00-7b9a-582e-bb36-014f084a08d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & -\\sqrt{3}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099611} {:answer/id #uuid "19e549cb-f70f-5feb-a295-b0871f09f0a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\sqrt{3} \\\\ -3.2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099612} {:answer/id #uuid "481625fa-4152-5af0-8d28-f2e247bb3b2b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{5} & 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/r